# spendless — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `bun` loads `.env` automatically, so `bun run spike`, `bun run seed` and
# `bun run capture` all pick these up. Vitest does not — the test suites use
# their own doubles and must never read a real credential.
#
# Nothing here belongs in a committed file. See AGENTS.md → Agent tooling.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PayPal sandbox (merchant side)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# From developer.paypal.com → Apps & Credentials → Sandbox → your app.
# Use the SANDBOX tab, not Live. Credentials are rotated per app, so if you
# created a second app for a US business account this is that one's pair.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional. An exported access token wins over the client-credentials pair,
# which is how the MCP server is driven. Tokens last roughly 8-9 hours in
# sandbox, so prefer the client ID + secret unless you have a reason.
# PAYPAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Sandbox only; `live` is not supported by this build and setting it
# is almost certainly a mistake.
# PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# Optional. Currency the seed charges in. USD is correct for a US account.
# Kept as a variable because it is the thing that caused
# UNSUPPORTED_PAYEE_CURRENCY, and that should be a one-line change, not a hunt.
# SEED_CURRENCY=USD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter (the agent)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# openrouter.ai → account → API keys. This is the AI half of the two hard
# eligibility requirements in AGENTS.md, so the build cannot honestly claim a
# meaningful AI integration without it.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. A cheap instruct model. Small with a tight schema beats a large one
# wandering — see todo.md H2-02. Both IDs below were verified against
# OpenRouter's live /api/v1/models on 2026-10-17, with real per-token prices.
#
#   default  meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct      $0.05/M in, $0.08/M out, 131k ctx
#   upgrade  mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b        $0.09/M in, $0.25/M out, 256k ctx
#
# A demo run is roughly 5k in + 1k out, so the default lands under $0.001 per
# run. Upgrade only if proposals come back weak — the agent only classifies and
# drafts rationale, so it is not the bottleneck.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct

# Optional. Caps the agent's spend per run. Small on purpose: the agent
# classifies and drafts rationale, it never computes a figure or moves money.
# OPENROUTER_MAX_SPEND_USD=0.05
